    "text": "What was life like at every rank in a German Panzer Division during WW2?\n\nThis animated WW2 POV history follows 18 ranks, from a young Panzerschütze inside a tank crew to Generalfeldmarschall at the top of the German Army.\n\nFollow German Panzer crews and commanders through Normandy, Falaise, the Ardennes, the Rhine crossing, the Ruhr Pocket, and the final collapse of Germany in 1945.\n\nSee how pay, tank crew responsibilities, fuel shortages, battlefield losses, and command decisions change as you rise from loading shells to commanding entire formations.\n\n⏱️ CHAPTERS\n\n00:00 — Panzerschütze\n00:50 — Gefreiter\n01:55 — Obergefreiter\n02:48 — Unteroffizier\n03:46 — Feldwebel\n04:44 — Oberfeldwebel\n05:42 — Stabsfeldwebel\n06:35 — Leutnant\n07:32 — Oberleutnant\n08:37 — Hauptmann\n09:31 — Major\n10:35 — Oberstleutnant\n11:48 — Oberst\n12:46 — Generalmajor\n13:39 — Generalleutnant\n14:47 — General der Panzertruppe\n15:52 — Generaloberst\n16:41 — Generalfeldmarschall\n\n📚 REFERENCES\n\nGerman Army (1935–1945) — rank and pay scale\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_...)\n\nPanzerworld — Wehrmacht Salaries\nhttps://panzerworld.com/wehrmacht-sal...\n\nGerman Army Salary Breakdown\nhttps://www.scribd.com/doc/115190494/...\n\nSenior Wehrmacht officer payments and historical study\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bribery...\nhttps://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi...\n\nRuhr Pocket — April 1945\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruhr_po...\nhttps://www.nationalww2museum.org/war...\n\nGerman surrender — May 1945\nhttps://www.archives.gov/milestone-do...\nhttps://time.com/3876923/germany-surr...\n\nPanzer Division 1944 organization and tank-company structure\nhttps://blog.sturmpanzer.com/panzer-d...\nhttps://feldgrau.net/forum/viewtopic....\n\nGerman Mark IV tank crew and communications\nhttps://www.lonesentry.com/articles/t...\n\nGerman Army NCO ranks and insignia\nhttps://www.bundeswehr.de/en/about-bu...\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranks_a...)\n\nCharacters and individual incidents are dramatized for historical storytelling. The video is based on historical ranks, military organization, equipment, pay references, and World War II campaigns.\n\n#WW2 #GermanArmy #PanzerDivision #MilitaryHistory #WW2History #POVHistory",
